  "source_call_graph": [
    "Qt Window file dialog -> CoreController::loadState(filename); LoadSaveState slot dialog -> CoreController::loadState(slot).",
    "The tested original QIODevice overload calls VFileDevice::wrap; the tested filename overload calls VFileDevice::open. Both capture a backup, call mCoreLoadStateNamed on the core thread, emit frameAvailable/stateLoaded only on true, and close their temporary input VFile after the callback.",
    "VFileDevice::open is the original pinned forwarder; this harness substitutes only VFileOpen with a Qt QBuffer fixture, then executes the original filename CoreController method and wrapper close path.",
    "VFileDevice::wrap opens the caller-owned QIODevice and returns null on open failure; its abstract VFile wrapper delegates read/seek and close closes the QIODevice then deletes the wrapper.",
    "mCoreLoadStateNamed returns false when mCoreExtractState cannot produce fixed-size state; this source branch has no direct log call. The Qt load slot has no explicit false-result signal.",
    "Qt LogController presentation remains filter/sink/category dependent; the Qt-category error dialog is not evidence that savestate failures are presented.",
    "SDL's optional state path opens a VFile, runs _loadState on the core thread, ignores mCoreLoadStateNamed's bool, and closes the VFile."
  ],
